  "last_activity_at": "2026-07-24T19:36:18.123Z",
  "latest_note": "server.ts wraps every route (and the fetch fallback) in guardHost(): a request whose Host header isn't localhost/127.0.0.1/[::1] gets 403, blocking DNS rebinding against the loopback-bound server. New tests/acceptance/web-host-header-allowlist.test.ts uses node:http (fetch forbids overriding Host) to prove foreign hosts 403, the DNS-rebinding shape (foreign hostname + real port) 403s, and localhost/127.0.0.1/[::1] still work. Full verification suite green (one unrelated pre-existing flaky test filed as t-eqidx).",
